{
  "title": "Lesson 19. The DOM",
  "description": "The page tree, querySelector, textContent, style, classList",
  "learn": {
    "intro": "Hi! Lesson 19 — the **DOM**. Until now JavaScript lived in the console. Today we learn to find page elements and change them. Let's go!",
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "What the DOM is",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🌳",
            "text": "The browser turns your HTML into a **tree of objects**. JavaScript can read this tree and change it. This is where JS becomes the brain of the site."
          },
          {
            "text": "The tree:",
            "code": "html\n └── body\n      └── div\n           └── p"
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "truefalse",
            "topic": "DOM",
            "prompt": "The DOM is a tree of objects the browser builds from HTML.",
            "answer": true,
            "explain": "JavaScript works with exactly this tree."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "querySelector and querySelectorAll",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🔍",
            "text": "`querySelector` finds the **first** element. The syntax is as in CSS (selectors from lesson 3).",
            "code": "const title = document.querySelector(\".card h2\");"
          },
          {
            "text": "`querySelectorAll` finds **all** elements:",
            "code": "const cards = document.querySelectorAll(\".card\");\ncards.forEach((card) => {\n  console.log(card);\n});"
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "Finding elements",
            "prompt": "Which method finds ALL the cards?",
            "options": [
              "querySelectorAll",
              "querySelector",
              "getAll",
              "find"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "querySelectorAll returns all matching elements."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Text and styles",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "✏️",
            "text": "Change the text:",
            "code": "const paragraph = document.querySelector(\"p\");\nparagraph.textContent = \"New text\";"
          },
          {
            "text": "Change the styles:",
            "code": "const title = document.querySelector(\"h1\");\ntitle.style.color = \"red\";"
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "Text and styles",
            "prompt": "How do you change the text of element el?",
            "options": [
              "el.textContent = \"текст\"",
              "el.text(\"текст\")",
              "el.write(\"текст\")",
              "el = \"текст\""
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "The textContent property holds the element's text."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Classes: add, remove, toggle",
        "slides": [
          {
            "emoji": "🔀",
            "text": "Classes through `classList`:",
            "code": "menu.classList.add(\"active\");     // add\nmenu.classList.remove(\"active\");  // remove\nmenu.classList.toggle(\"active\");  // switch"
          },
          {
            "quote": true,
            "text": "`toggle`: if the class is there it removes it, if not it adds it. Perfect for a menu: click — opens, click again — closes."
          },
          {
            "text": "Homework: a script that finds all landing cards with `querySelectorAll` and adds a bordered class when the page loads."
          }
        ],
        "check": [
          {
            "type": "choice",
            "topic": "classList",
            "prompt": "What does classList.toggle(\"active\") do?",
            "options": [
              "Adds the class if absent and removes it if present",
              "Always adds the class",
              "Always removes the class",
              "Changes the color"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explain": "toggle switches the class."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
